{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#!/usr/bin/python3\n\ndef is_good(f, p, k):\n    for i in range(p):\n        if f[(k * i) % p] != (k * f[i]) % p:\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef gen(f, p, k, i):\n    if i == p:\n        return is_good(f, p, k)\n    else:\n        ans = 0\n        for j in range(p):\n            f.append(j)\n            ans += gen(f, p, k, i + 1)\n            f.pop()\n        return ans\n\ndef solve(p, k):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    num = 0\n    visited = [False] * p\n    for start in range(p):\n        if not visited[start]:\n            num += 1\n            current = start\n            while not visited[current]:\n                visited[current] = True\n                current = (current * k) % p\n    exp = num - (0 if k == 1 else 1)\n    return pow(p, exp, MOD)\n\np, k = map(int, input().split())\nprint(solve(p, k))\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int p = scanner.nextInt();\n        int k = scanner.nextInt();\n        System.out.println(solve(p, k));\n    }\n\n    public static long solve(int p, int k) {\n        long MOD = 1000000007;\n        int num = 0;\n        boolean[] visited = new boolean[p];\n        \n        for (int start = 0; start < p; start++) {\n            if (!visited[start]) {\n                num++;\n                int current = start;\n                while (!visited[current]) {\n                    visited[current] = true;\n                    current = (int) ((long) current * k % p);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        int exp = num - (k == 1 ? 0 : 1);\n        return powMod(p, exp, MOD);\n    }\n\n    public static long powMod(int base, int exp, long mod) {\n        long result = 1;\n        long b = base % mod;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) {\n                result = (result * b) % mod;\n            }\n            b = (b * b) % mod;\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-8.844937838148326e-05, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.802703940891661e-05, -9.536697689327411e-06, -0.0006400682032108307, -0.14714279770851135, -5.602820692729438e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -5.435795901576057e-05, -0.20141363143920898, -0.011050336994230747, -0.04332587495446205, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.011435911059379578, -4.088794958079234e-05, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -1.311301275563892e-06, -2.2649508537142538e-05, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -3.099393507000059e-05, -0.5786746144294739, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.6689160474925302e-05, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -7.510157047363464e-06, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -0.048605382442474365, 0.0, 0.0, -3.659658250398934e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -4.8